\title{CyteTypeR: CyteType for R}
\description{
CyteTypeR is the R client of CyteType, an agentic, evidence-based cell type
annotation service for single-cell RNA-seq data. It prepares a clustered
Seurat object and its marker genes, submits an annotation job to the
CyteType API and adds the results to the object: a cell type label, a Cell
Ontology term, a cell state and the reviewer's confidence for every
cluster. Every job also produces an interactive report.
}
\section{Workflow}{

\enumerate{
\item Sign in once per computer with \code{\link[=SetupCyteTypeR]{SetupCyteTypeR()}}, or save an API key
you already have with \code{\link[=LoginCyteTypeR]{LoginCyteTypeR()}}.
\item Run \code{\link[=PrepareCyteTypeR]{PrepareCyteTypeR()}} on a normalized, clustered Seurat object and the
marker table from \code{Seurat::FindAllMarkers()}.
\item Run \code{\link[=CyteTypeR]{CyteTypeR()}} to upload the data, submit the job, wait for it and add
the results to the object.
\item Use \code{\link[=GetResults]{GetResults()}} to read the results again, or to fetch the results of
a job by its ID, and \code{\link[=CleanUpArtifacts]{CleanUpArtifacts()}} to delete the uploaded files.
}

\code{\link[=OpenCyteTypeDashboard]{OpenCyteTypeDashboard()}} and \code{\link[=ViewCyteTypeJob]{ViewCyteTypeJob()}} open the dashboard and a
job's report. \code{\link[=InstallCyteTypeRCli]{InstallCyteTypeRCli()}} installs the \code{cytetyper} terminal
command, which signs in and opens reports from a shell.
}

\section{Documentation}{

The CyteType documentation at \url{https://docs.nygen.io/CyteType/} covers both
